{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold","id":692431,"title":"Tarot Card Freehold","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-07T07:18:16-07:00","id":692431,"title":"Tarot Card Freehold","content":"So I have this idea for a freehold, its courts centered around the 4 Suits (Pentacle, Cup, Sword, Wand), and whose bulwark is either a yearly reading of the cards, which the freehold must either make a reality by next year, or endure therein. Question is: how would governance work? Would there be four kings/queens ruling simultaneously, or only 1? Also, would certain members of the freehold become representatives of particular (major) arcana, or gain boons symbolic of said-cards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:44:39-07:00","id":692629,"title":"","content":"It sounds like a cool idea. Maybe governance is determined yearly, with whichever suit is most represented in the oracular spread taking control of (and responsibility for) the Freehold. As far as I know, there aren't really correspondences between the Major and Minor Arcana, but they might make for interesting Entitlements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:55:20-07:00","id":692641,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, the Wyrd might choose from among the freehold's members to represent one of the major arcana. Hell, maybe each motley gets a reading as well, needing to complete their own task on pain of adding difficulty to the Freehold Reading. (Maybe per successful motely adds or subtracts a card?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:44:19-07:00","id":692714,"title":"","content":"Well, the Major Arcana tell the story of The Fool's journey from ignorance to enlightenment. Maybe part of the bulwark is a single member of the freehold taking on the role of the Fool, and going through their own Fool's Journey throughout the course of the year? Maybe the reading tells him or her certain steps that must be taken along the way. Then, people who aid the Fool along their journey might be selected by the Wyrd for other major arcana roles based on the assistance they gave him or her. So, for example, someone who offered the Fool spiritual guidance might become the Hierophant (as opposed to a pre-selected Hierophant being obligated to give the Fool spiritual advice).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-07-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:06:55-07:00","id":692736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=692714#post692714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, people who aid the Fool along their journey might be selected by the Wyrd for other major arcana roles based on the assistance they gave him or her. So, for example, someone who offered the Fool spiritual guidance might become the Hierophant (as opposed to a pre-selected Hierophant being obligated to give the Fool spiritual advice).</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Bulwark is broken if Fool's Journey goes in wrong order - after meeting Magician, Fool need to see High Priestess. But if he cross his paths with Hermit then, Gentry has open way in to world. And so Lords and Ladies send Huntsman to Tarot Freehold to break Fool's Journey and assume persona of wrong Major Arcana...<br /> <br /> So much fairy tale stories can be said about this model!<br /> <br /> <b>Side note:</b> I assume that Fool is practical equivalent of Highest Monarch in Seasons and similar Court Systems?<br /> <br /> Or maybe Fool <i>must</i> be the changeling that was the <b>shortest</b> time in Freehold, on Earth, just from the Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:09:31-07:00","id":692738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=692714#post692714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Major Arcana tell the story of The Fool's journey from ignorance to enlightenment. Maybe part of the bulwark is a single member of the freehold taking on the role of the Fool, and going through their own Fool's Journey throughout the course of the year? Maybe the reading tells him or her certain steps that must be taken along the way. Then, people who aid the Fool along their journey might be selected by the Wyrd for other major arcana roles based on the assistance they gave him or her. So, for example, someone who offered the Fool spiritual guidance might become the Hierophant (as opposed to a pre-selected Hierophant being obligated to give the Fool spiritual advice).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the problem with that is it means going through all the 78 cards (or 22 major arcana). Sort of defeats the excitement and uncertainty of having a Reading, which ranges between 3, to 5, to 7 or (in the Celtic Cross) 10 cards. That is, unless you're saying someone in the freehold has to offer themselves up to getting their fortune told, thereby becoming the target of whatever becomes ordained. How then, does the Wyld Hunt occur? Kill the target? Or ensure the prophecy fails?<br /> <br /> Edit: Wyrdhamster ninjad me. xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 10-07-2015, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:16:04-07:00","id":692744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=692736#post692736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Bulwark is broken if Fool's Journey goes in wrong order - after meeting Magician, Fool need to see High Priestess. But if he cross his paths with Hermit then, Gentry has open way in to world. And so Lords and Ladies send Huntsman to Tarot Freehold to break Fool's Journey and assume persona of wrong Major Arcana...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, I wouldn't make it quite that rigidly structured, otherwise every Fool's Journey would end up looking the same every year. Rather, I would say that the Journey must be personal to each Fool that undertakes it, but it also must include all of the events foretold in the initial oracular reading, or else the bulwark is broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=692736#post692736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Side note:</b> I assume that Fool is practical equivalent of Highest Monarch in Seasons and similar Court Systems?<br /> <br /> Or maybe Fool <i>must</i> be the changeling that was the <b>shortest</b> time in Freehold, on Earth, just from the Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say something more like the latter. Maybe not necessarily the newest member of the freehold, or else it would end up being the same person most years. I would just say the Fool has to be someone who hasn't realized their full potential, and volunteers for the role. Probably someone not associated with one of the four suit courts, though I'm not sure that would technically be a requirement. It would surely be both a tremendous honor and a grave responsibility. I could also see it ending up very Hunger Games, what with the Courts selecting a mandatory &quot;volunteer&quot; from the courtless every year.<br /> <br /> As for the Monarchs, I would say each Court has a King, a Queen, a Knight, and a Page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-07-2015, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:18:23-07:00","id":692747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=692744#post692744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh, I wouldn't make it quite that rigidly structured, otherwise every Fool's Journey would end up looking the same every year. Rather, I would say that the Journey must be personal to each Fool that undertakes it, but it also must include all of the events foretold in the initial oracular reading, or else the bulwark is broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say something more like the latter. Maybe not necessarily the newest member of the freehold, or else it would end up being the same person most years. I would just say the Fool has to be someone who hasn't realized their full potential. Probably someone not associated with one of the comfort suit courts, though I'm not sure that would technically be a requirement, who volunteers for the role. It would surely be both a tremendous honor and a grave responsibility.<br /> <br /> As for the Monarchs, I would say each Court has a King, a Queen, a Knight, and a Page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps there's a lottery? Only the &quot;face cards&quot; are exempt from them (to ensure stability). Can't have your king running around when he's needed for administration duties. Hence why the jobs are so desired, if only to avoid the possible danger surrounding the cards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:26:42-07:00","id":692755,"title":"","content":"This lottery looks very much like this? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e3PJ3Du_zDc\" data-code=\"e3PJ3Du_zDc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/e3PJ3Du_zDc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:28:09-07:00","id":692756,"title":"","content":"Haha look at my edit. It seems we all had the same idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:13:29-07:00","id":692790,"title":"","content":"The only problem I have with Tarot Card Freehold, that it marks only one character as Fool - and <b>Changeling</b> games are about whole motleys. The one character as most important to the group is risky game design.<br /> <br /> Maybe there is a way to have multiple Fool characters in one group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:27:34-07:00","id":692835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=692790#post692790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem I have with Tarot Card Freehold, that it marks only one character as Fool - and <b>Changeling</b> games are about whole motleys. The one character as most important to the group is risky game design.<br /> <br /> Maybe there is a way to have multiple Fool characters in one group?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's assuming the Fool's Journey is the focus of the chronicle. The PCs could easily be a group of Courtiers playing the political game and trying to influence The Fool to suit their agendas. Or a motley of Courtless, maybe some of them even former Fools, rebelling against the Courts and their tyrannical lottery system. Maybe each player has a Major Arcana role and are playing an equal role in the Bulwark as the Fool (there's no rule against that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:45:12-07:00","id":692880,"title":"","content":"I also think that other variant could be that Lottery takes place in all (Minor) Arcana Courts and in Courtless - each one of the Fools is treated as possible candidate, but the one that <b>survives</b> to the end, is real winner.<br /> <br /> ( Yes, survive like in <i>Hunger Games</i> - in this take Wyrd is actively hunting Fools to limit the to one only at the end and Gentry is obvious to mark them as their victims. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <b>I think we have strong idea for general Bulwark - now, could someone write Arcana Courts in 2ED format?</b><br /> <br /> I can add from myself that in White Wolf forums times there were fan created <b><i>Tarot for Willpower</i></b> rules that I use in mine <b>Mage</b> games to this day - only that I have mine Polish translation, not original document. There were nice, open interpretations for all &quot;Colors&quot; so maybe look in there could be. I will do quick translate for this topic on general sum up from mine files. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I will also ask openly on general forum for original rules, maybe someone have them in English <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> <b>Wands/ Sticks/ Clubs/ Fire / Creativity </b><br /> Psychic Sphere \u2014 Wands represent idea, they are original seeds or ideas and most important - elements of development. When we see Wands in play, they point to the ideas, ambitions and growth.<br /> <i>Sphere:</i> Mental Skills<br /> <br /> <b>Cups/ Chalices/ Hearts/ Water/ Passion</b><br /> Heart Sphere \u2014 Cups represent strength and power to achieve by will alone. When we see Cups in play, they point on needs and feelings, and to overcoming strives in obtaining them.<br /> <i>Sphere:</i> Resolve, Stamina, Composure or Defense<br /> <br /> <b>Swords/ Sabers/ Air/ Actions </b><br /> Action Sphere \u2014 Swords represent focused will to make physical manifestation. Often Swords means combat; difficulties in making physical ideas in to reality. When we see Swords in play, they point to action and conflict before final resolution.<br /> <i>Sphere:</i> Physical Skills<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacles/ Coins/ Diamonds/ Earth/ Charm</b><br /> Social Sphere \u2013 Pentacles represent our material desires and social standing. Coins are manifestation of material plane, body, fruits of our work and gifts, we desire. When we see Pentacles in play, they point not only on wealth and power, but also on social manipulation and actual results.<br /> <i>Sphere:</i> Social Skills<br /> <br /> So who made those in to proper 2ED Courts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T06:42:06-07:00","id":693815,"title":"","content":"Regarding the bulwark, an alternative would be to target a single mortal (determined by the Wyrd) within the territory of the freehold. Failure to complete the fortune risks that mortal being taken by the Gentry? In addition to the territory becoming open season for the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T06:54:45-07:00","id":693826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=693815#post693815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the bulwark, an alternative would be to target a single mortal (determined by the Wyrd) within the territory of the freehold. Failure to complete the fortune risks that mortal being taken by the Gentry? In addition to the territory becoming open season for the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T07:03:44-07:00","id":693833,"title":"","content":"Idea for Major Arcana-could they be positions in Courts? Emperor/Empress is ruler,Magician some version of court mage or most experienced in Contracts, Hermit lore-keeper, High Priestess/Hieroprath best at Pledge-craft or dealing with other supernatural threats...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T07:20:45-07:00","id":693843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>coolcat12345</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=693833#post693833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea for Major Arcana-could they be positions in Courts? Emperor/Empress is ruler, Magician some version of court mage or most experienced in Contracts, Hermit lore-keeper, High Priestess/Hieroprath best at Pledge-craft or dealing with other supernatural threats...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is: would the freehold have enough people for that? There's also a LOT of ways to interpret a single arcana. Might be too much stress limiting it to a single job or person.<br /> <br /> Another thought occurs: suppose the bulwark is too easy. If you manage to get all the omens done in a week, that's an entire year done. So, what if the number of cards determines length of sanctuary? A 3 card read equals 1 month and a day (which is also the deadline). 5 cards equals a season. 7 is half a year, and 10 is a full one. That is, unless the changelings don't KNOW who the target is, which adds to the difficulty. You gotta track 'em down and make sure they're the one, otherwise times're wasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T08:50:16-07:00","id":693891,"title":"","content":"Assume that a freehold has enough changelings to warrant the design it has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T08:59:31-07:00","id":693896,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. The Wyrd would probably then alter the mantle of appropriate freehold members. Not sure what that'd mean stat-wise. Maybe just a boost to social rolls in the freehold? (Though I'll admit, that might be a bit passe.) Might be better off representing the Majors as an entitlement. I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:10:05-07:00","id":693910,"title":"","content":"This, by the way, is a fascinating little exercise in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:47:14-07:00","id":693966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=693815#post693815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the bulwark, an alternative would be to target a single mortal (determined by the Wyrd) within the territory of the freehold. Failure to complete the fortune risks that mortal being taken by the Gentry? In addition to the territory becoming open season for the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rolling with this idea, maybe the goal is to lead this mortal down a particular path (again, determined by the reading), but certain members of the freehold can only interact with them in certain ways, as determined by their major arcana role. The Empress can only offer the Fool maternal advice. The Devil can only tempt and manipulate the Fool. The Chariot can only offer the Fool transportation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:42:36-07:00","id":694011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/692431-tarot-card-freehold?p=693843#post693843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought occurs: suppose the bulwark is too easy. If you manage to get all the omens done in a week, that's an entire year done. So, what if the number of cards determines length of sanctuary? A 3 card read equals 1 month and a day (which is also the deadline). 5 cards equals a season. 7 is half a year, and 10 is a full one. That is, unless the changelings don't KNOW who the target is, which adds to the difficulty. You gotta track 'em down and make sure they're the one, otherwise times're wasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have the number of cards equal the number of days (weeks if preferred) that are allowed to finish with each omen and the cards are only turned over one at a time to determine the next omen or the cards are blank until an omen is reached. Technically, it could be done very quickly, but practically, it would take a fair amount of time. It would work well for a story anyway, each card representing a game session. It would allow for mixed results, so if the changelings can't take care of one or some they won't completely fail.<br /> <br /> The length of time could be a year after the read is resolved or the number of days, or weeks, of the number of cards times the number of cards. 3 x 3 = 9, 5 x 5 = 25, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-08-2015, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T20:50:50-07:00","id":694486,"title":"","content":"I'm not an expert on Changeling and I know jack about the tarot, but how about this for an idea; a motely is chosen by lottery and they then witness the play of the cards but the reading is for some innocent (and ignorant) mortal within the bounds of the freehold. Now the motely's role is to ensure the fool completes his journey (starting by finding him) while the huntsman work to stop him. To think in terms of Alice in Wonderland, Alice is the fool while the characters take on the roles of the white rabbit, mad hatter and Cheshire cat. The huntsman become the walrus, caterpillar and red queen. If the motely succeeds then the freehold is protected, if they fail then the red queen herself is free to act outside of the reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}